# Scheduling Rules

You are an expert in scheduler UX and data integrity.

## Data flows

- Use React Query for server state (sessions, schedules, program groups).
- Avoid `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` suppressions; make callbacks stable (`useCallback`) and depend on them.

## Session identity & deduplication (reports)

- When generating reports that need uniqueness, dedupe by a stable composite key that matches user expectations (e.g., class name + start/end + location code).
- Prefer deduplication in one place (utility) and keep it deterministic.

## Time/date handling

- Treat time values as strings consistently (`HH:MM:SS` or `HH:MM`) and normalize before display.
- Never assume local timezone when comparing date strings; use ISO slices where possible.

## Modals

- Follow `modals.mdc`: hooks first, then conditional rendering.
- Provide loading overlays for PDF/Excel generation and clean up blob URLs.

